WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.775
NULLIF is also useful for numeric safety Division by
zero is an

00:00:04.800 --> 00:00:10.525
error and the practice data includes a zero bill
NULLIF bill_amount zero

00:00:10.550 --> 00:00:15.725
converts an exact zero denominator to NULL Division
by NULL then returns

00:00:15.750 --> 00:00:19.812
NULL rather than raising an error Here that means
the percentage is

00:00:19.825 --> 00:00:25.150
not computable which is different from zero percent
The numerator uses COALESCE

00:00:25.175 --> 00:00:29.425
amount_paid to zero which is a separate assumption
that should be justified

00:00:29.438 --> 00:00:33.562
by the domain Run the query and inspect the No
Charge record

00:00:34.438 --> 00:00:37.950
Safe SQL should avoid errors while preserving the
meaning of the data
